      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T19:58:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should we consider to move this above to exit earlier? e.g. to line 5817",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81aef701_7e1f6595",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T21:08:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "1. Keeping this check here makes sure that we are complaining about the missing callback only when the DSA is used.\n2. Presently, DSA data consumer is registered during initialization by the HOGP. However, LE audio client should not make any assumptions about it. It is possible that HOGP or any other consumer would register this callback only when the DSA is activated.",
      "parentUuid": "f9084889_79b20635",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b290067d_7a473c1a",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1981586
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T21:12:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not suggesting to remove this check. \nJust from the code logic flow\u0027s pov, I think it would be better to do this check earlier than here, so that if callback is null, we skip checking the rest.",
      "parentUuid": "81aef701_7e1f6595",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e87da06a_8361b473",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-28T21:54:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is an error if DSA active but the callback is not registered. We should log if this happens. If we return early, we don\u0027t know if DSA was active or not. So we cannot determine if this was an error or not.",
      "parentUuid": "b290067d_7a473c1a",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "59a019b8_d623e296",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1929540
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-29T17:41:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so the sytuation that `iso_data_callback \u003d\u003d nullptr` and dsa_ is active is OK or Not ?\n\nWhen this function returns false, data will be considered as audio data - is this expected?\n\nMaybe we should have here `return true` ?",
      "parentUuid": "e87da06a_8361b473",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3daacdae_d0d7d9dc",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-29T17:59:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Returning true might break non-DSA usecases if the DSA states were set wrong.",
      "parentUuid": "59a019b8_d623e296",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7782e8bb_74f6d426",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1928988
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-05T10:22:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Seeing both arguments, it seems to me that we either interpret the DSA data as audio if callback is not registered but DSA mode enabled, or we interpret the audio data as DSA if DSA states were set wrong for the non-DSA usecase. If I understand correctly, in either case the behavior would be invalid due to potential logical error in the code (misconfiguration), so maybe we should assert if the two are misconfigured (callback vs DSA mode)?",
      "parentUuid": "3daacdae_d0d7d9dc",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e742d06a_0b5bda61",
        "filename": "system/bta/le_audio/client.cc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 5831,
      "author": {
        "id": 1882530
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-03-06T01:27:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO assert should be used only when the system cannot be recovered from the error.\n\nThat aside, I want to take a step back and go through all the concerns raised here.\n\n1. Should we fail earlier by moving the check for the iso_data_callback earlier?\nMissing callback when DSA was active is an error which should be logged. We will be aware of this error only when we have confirmed that the DSA was active. So I think this is an appropriate place for this check.\n\n2. Should we return true if DSA is active?\nIf DSA was mistakenly active, it may be possible that the iso callback is missing and audio data is lost.\nIf DSA was mistakenly not active, the receiver state check will prevent the headtracking data from getting treated as audio data. This is the condition, that led this cl.\n\n\nIrrespective of which way one may lean, I don\u0027t think these concerns should block this cl. We can improve this logic later.",
      "parentUuid": "7782e8bb_74f6d426",
      "revId": "4e056503a998a317e899ff22342087f583d0e1e6",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
  ]
